architecture connection-source-catalog
  canonical_name ConnectionSourceCatalog
  family identity
  domain Identity / Connection Discovery
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Which retained connection source candidates can be inspected with their original coordinates?
  purpose Read paginated connection candidates from retained local Parquet projections and check each candidate against its original source row before returning it.
  maturity implemented
  publishes ConnectionSourceCandidate
  source_path cmd/BonfyreConnectionCatalog/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreConnectionCatalog/tests/catalog_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/connections_workspace.h
  source_path integrations/browser/connection-studio.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/connections_workspace.test.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreConnectionCatalog/tests/catalog_test.sh checks bounded pagination, parameterized name search, ecosystem filtering, non-clickable HTTP addresses, private-field omission in the app view, duplicate coordinates across ecosystems, altered source entries and refusal without partial output
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/connections_workspace.test.mjs checks current-account admission, refusal of other accounts and caller-supplied paths, reduced output, search and an installed Chrome workspace using the same endpoint
  invariant every returned candidate has a unique source coordinate and matching source row digest, and its source entry appears in that row
  invariant the CLI reads explicit local files; its default view contains private source coordinates, while its app view emits only ecosystem, name, safe HTTPS link and candidate status. Neither view is an account-facing endpoint or an authorization boundary
  forbidden_inference a source candidate or HTTPS locator -> provider ownership, current availability, permission to connect, installed capability, license or authorization
  invariant the account endpoint reads only configured absolute source paths, requires the configured current personal actor and subject, and refuses private source coordinates in its reduced output
  known_gap the account endpoint and Connection Studio panel require a release with the native reader, DuckDB library and retained source snapshots configured; source entries remain unverified candidates

interaction connection-studio-reads-source-catalog
  source cmd-web-address
  destination connection-source-catalog
  relation requests
  preserves exact authenticated personal account, bounded pagination, ecosystem and literal name search, candidate status and safe HTTPS locator
  drops private goal coordinates, original lines, arbitrary source paths and any implied provider authorization
  forbidden_inference a catalog entry or source locator -> installed connector, ownership, provider consent or permission to act
  invalidates_on account session, configured subject, retained source snapshots or native reader changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/connections_workspace.test.mjs
